From 590a18f75f0913be17c876a51b90dffc68fbc13f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: engmessias <vmessiaswt@gmailcom>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:38:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(fleet): close S6 review findings on the B15a.2 series
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- replay: bounded pagination — serve the largest prefix that fits the 8 KiB
  envelope with an advancing next_cursor (was a dead-end payload_too_large
  retry loop for backlogs beyond ~31 events); payload_too_large is now a
  canonical bounded ERROR_CODES member.
- session_ended(session_ref=...) and the hooks/funnel chain carry the closed
  session id: an ended session's association is torn down even when the
  resolver already moved on, and closes of unrelated sessions are no-ops.
- cursor MAC compare on bytes (str compare_digest raised on non-ASCII input);
  a hub-first expiry check surfaces as cursor_expired, not replay_gap.
- tests: session group 78 passed (+8); regression 216; ruff clean.
